	(text "The pot side of each chip (U7A, U8A, U9A) is drawn on the audio sheets where it acts.\nV+ = 9V and V- = GND, so the pot ends can swing anywhere from 0V to 9V.\nVL = 3.3V matches the microcontroller's logic.  WLAT tied low: a new setting takes effect at once.\nSHDN tied high: normal operation.  At power-up each wiper starts at mid-scale until the\nmicrocontroller restores the saved setting.\n\nNote: the datasheet specifies the analog side from V+ = 10V.  At about 8.6V it still works\n(it resets below 6V) but the wiper resistance is higher: about 150 ohms instead of 75,\nwhich R4 on the Input and Gain sheet allows for.  Confirm on the breadboard."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 144.78 0)
		(effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left))
		(uuid "e9054bf2-9a5e-425a-b695-2db47ebee9e5")
	)
